THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The license above covers the source code of digital-bypass only.

The bundled zapret-discord-youtube build (winws2, WinDivert, Lua scripts,
lists and strategies) is distributed under the licenses of its respective
authors; see LICENSE.txt inside the bundled build folder.

Rust and JavaScript dependencies (Tauri, rustls, Svelte and others) are used
under their own licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, ISC and similar), all compatible
with GPL-3.0.

The Telegram module is a Rust port of tg-ws-proxy by Flowseal (MIT),
https://github.com/Flowseal/tg-ws-proxy; the built-in Cloudflare Worker script
and the default CF proxy domain list come from that project.

The proxy auto mode and OOB technique are inspired by ByeDPI by hufrea (MIT),
https://github.com/hufrea/byedpi; the code is original.

The SNI scanner idea comes from sni-spoofing-rust by therealaleph (MIT),
https://github.com/therealaleph/sni-spoofing-rust; the code is original.

digital-bypass is based on Zapret2-RustGUI by the same author
(https://github.com/digital-bombyx/Zapret2-RustGUI). Earlier releases of
Zapret2-RustGUI remain available under the MIT License.

Ideas without copied code (credited as a courtesy): NoDPI by GVCoder09
(GPL-3.0), https://github.com/GVCoder09/NoDPI; SpoofDPI by xvzc (Apache-2.0),
https://github.com/xvzc/spoofdpi; GreenTunnel by Sadegh Hayeri (MIT),
https://github.com/SadeghHayeri/GreenTunnel; zapret by bol-van,
https://github.com/bol-van/zapret (blockcheck methodology, --wssize and
--ssid-filter ideas).

zapret2 add-ons (src-tauri/addons): zapret-auto.lua and the WinDivert filter
parts come from zapret-win-bundle by bol-van (MIT, Copyright (c) 2016-2026
bol-van), https://github.com/bol-van/zapret2. Monkey64.sys is an unmodified
copy of WinDivert64.sys and WinDivert-monkey.dll a patched WinDivert.dll from
the same bundle; WinDivert by basil00 is licensed under LGPL-3.0 / GPL-2.0,
https://github.com/basil00/WinDivert.

Strategies "general (K-*).bat" (src-tauri/addons/strats) come from
zapret2-discord-youtube-strats by kinlay0 (MIT),
https://github.com/kinlay0/zapret2-discord-youtube-strats; fake names were
mapped to the Flowseal build, tls_clienthello_firpo_ru.bin and
tls_clienthello_retext_ai.bin with blobs-extra.lua come from the same project.

Tor (tor.exe) and lyrebird (obfs4, webtunnel, snowflake and meek transports)
are unmodified binaries from the Tor Expert Bundle by The Tor Project,
https://www.torproject.org/, downloaded from dist.torproject.org with a pinned
SHA-256 (scripts/sync-tor.mjs). Tor is distributed under the 3-clause BSD
license; lyrebird and its dependencies under BSD-style and other licenses.
The full license texts ship with the installer in the tor\docs folder.

Bridge lists for the bridge search are downloaded at run time from
Tor-Bridges-Collector-v2 by scriptzteam,
https://github.com/scriptzteam/Tor-Bridges-Collector-v2. The bridge search is
a Rust rewrite of TorBridgeMaster by the same author as digital-bypass,
https://github.com/digital-bombyx/TorBridgeMaster. The idea of giving Tor to
programs that do not support it comes from Tallow by basil00 (GPL-3.0),
https://github.com/basil00/Tallow; no code was copied.

